    "title": "Chris Brown & Usher announce El Paso stop for 'The R&B Tour' at Sun Bowl Stadium",
    "text": "EL PASO, Texas (KFOX14/CBS4) — After months of speculation, it’s official: two of R&B’s biggest names are joining forces for a highly anticipated tour stop in the Borderland. Chris Brown and Usher will bring “The R&B Tour” to Sun Bowl Stadium on Saturday, October 3, 2026, marking one of the most high-profile concert events to hit the region in recent years.The announcement confirms what fans have long expected—a collaboration between the chart-topping artists, both known for their decades-spanning influence on R&B, pop, and hip-hop. The tour branding, “Raymond & Brown,” nods to their surnames and signals a celebration of their legacies, hits, and stage presence.While full tour details are still rolling out, anticipation is already building across social media, with fans eager to see what the two performers have planned. Both artists are known for high-energy performances, intricate choreography, and extensive catalogs of hits, suggesting a show that will blend nostalgia with modern production.Fire in central El Paso ruled intentional, investigation openedOrganizers are urging fans to act quickly, as demand is expected to be high. Those interested in early ticket access can sign up now for the Artist Presale at RaymondAndBrownTour.com.The event is being presented in partnership with Live Nation and UTEP, bringing a major entertainment moment to Sun Bowl Stadium.RECOMMENDED: Ticketmaster releases additional BTS tickets at face value amid high demandSign up to receive the top interesting stories from in and around our community once daily in your inbox.",
